# The common positive fibre of all three actual boundary maps

Every original boundary-to-regular-family map agrees on its genuine Wang
fibre with the same normalized marked regular-family inclusion, in every
degree.  In degree four this common map is injective, by the actual kernel
theorem and the vanishing top-degree monodromy difference.
